    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- In your Project Planning Guide, respond to the question in **Step 5: Modeling**, under **Predicting, Evaluating, and Iterating**.\r\n- Use your model to get predictions from your test inputs.\r\n- Evaluate these predictions using the metrics of your choice.\r\n- Adjust your model’s hyperparameters to optimize for the metrics of your choice.\r\n\r\n💻 Coding Tip\r\n\r\nRemember you can use `model.predict` to get your models predictions from your test inputs—scaled if necessary.\r\n\r\n```\r\npredictions = model.predict(scaled_test_inputs)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso recall you can use `accuracy_score`, `recall_score`, and `precision_score` to assess your model’s accuracy, recall, and precision respectively.\r\n\r\n```\r\nprint(f\"Model Accuracy: {round(accuracy_score(test_outputs, predictions), 2)}\")\r\nprint(\r\n    f\"Model Recall: {round(recall_score(test_outputs, predictions, pos_label=\"LABEL\"), 2)}\"\r\n)\r\nprint(\r\n    f\"Model Precision: {round(precision_score(test_outputs, predictions, pos_label=\"LABEL\"), 2)}\"\r\n)\r\n```",
